    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0403" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/1433½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">22 March, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am much obliged to you
                    for sending these papers to me so promptly, but I do not find in them sufficient
                    cause for altering our position. They still do not answer the question I have
                    put to Lord Reading and to all others who argue in favour of intervention by
                    Japan, namely, What is it to effect and how will it be efficacious in effecting
                    it? The condition of Siberia furnishes no answer.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
